            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[1.1]</span> Under the **Yalta** and **Potsdam** agreements, both Germany and **Berlin**—located **100 miles** inside the Soviet eastern zone—were divided into **four occupation zones**. While **Stalin** stripped industrial reparations to keep Germany weak, Britain and the **United States** merged their zones economically into **Bizonia** in **January 1947** (joined by France to form **Trizonia** in **1948**) and channelled **Marshall Plan** aid into western German recovery.",
