          "title": "Source B: President John F. Kennedy’s Private Reflection After the Vienna Summit (4 June 1961)",
          "text": "Worst thing in my life. He savaged me... I think I know why he treated me like this. He thinks because of the Bay of Pigs that I’m inexperienced. Probably thinks I’m stupid. Maybe most important, he thinks that I had no guts... So we have got to see what we can do that will restore a feeling in Moscow that we will defend our national interests. I’ve got to show him swiftly—and Berlin is the place where he is going to test me.",
          "content": "Worst thing in my life. He savaged me... I think I know why he treated me like this. He thinks because of the Bay of Pigs that I’m inexperienced. Probably thinks I’m stupid. Maybe most important, he thinks that I had no guts... So we have got to see what we can do that will restore a feeling in Moscow that we will defend our national interests. I’ve got to show him swiftly—and Berlin is the place where he is going to test me.",
