            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[1.1]</span> For decades the **United States** treated **Cuba**—just **90 miles** south of Florida—as part of its economic backyard, backing corrupt military dictator **Fulgencio Batista** while American corporations owned most Cuban sugar plantations, oil refineries, railways, and electricity networks. In **January 1959**, nationalist guerrilla leader **Fidel Castro** and **Che Guevara** overthrew Batista and began nationalising US-owned land and businesses.",
