          "title": "Source A: The Czechoslovak Communist Party’s Action Programme (5 April 1968)",
          "text": "The Communist Party of Czechoslovakia builds on the voluntary support of the people; it cannot enforce its authority, this authority must be won again and again by Party activity. It cannot force its line through directives, but by the work of its members and the veracity of its ideals... Censorship prior to publication must be eliminated; freedom of expression even for minority interests must be guaranteed by law, while our foreign policy remains firmly anchored in alliance and cooperation with the Soviet Union and the other socialist states.",
          "content": "The Communist Party of Czechoslovakia builds on the voluntary support of the people; it cannot enforce its authority, this authority must be won again and again by Party activity. It cannot force its line through directives, but by the work of its members and the veracity of its ideals... Censorship prior to publication must be eliminated; freedom of expression even for minority interests must be guaranteed by law, while our foreign policy remains firmly anchored in alliance and cooperation with the Soviet Union and the other socialist states.",
