            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> In **June 1987**, speaking before West Berlin’s **Brandenburg Gate**, **Reagan** publicly challenged Moscow to prove its reformist sincerity: *\"Mr. Gorbachev, tear down this wall!\"* Meanwhile, Soviet scientists quietly advised **Gorbachev** that America’s **SDI** laser shield was technologically unproven and far cheaper to counter than to match, persuading him in **February 1987** to uncouple missile cuts from **SDI**.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Consequently, at the **Washington Summit** on **8 December 1987**, Reagan and Gorbachev signed the **Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces** (**INF Treaty**). Unlike **SALT 1**, which merely capped warhead growth, the **INF Treaty** eliminated an entire category of land-based nuclear and conventional missiles with ranges of **500 to 5,500 km**—destroying over **2,600** Soviet **SS-20** and US **Pershing II** and **Cruise** missiles under intrusive on-site inspections."
